---
import Layout from '../components/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Data Deletion | GoZeroShot"
  description="How to request deletion of data GoZeroShot holds from connected social-media accounts, and how that differs from removing already-published content."
>
  <main class="main legal-page">
    <section class="legal-shell">
      <a class="back-link" href="/">Back to home</a>
      <h1>Data Deletion</h1>
      <p class="effective-date">Last updated: September 21, 2026</p>

      <p>
        This page explains how to request deletion of data GoZeroShot holds
        after you connected a social-media or advertising account, and how
        that differs from removing content already published to a platform.
        See our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for the full details on
        what we collect and why.
      </p>

      <h2>How to request deletion</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:alynch@gozeroshot.dev">alynch@gozeroshot.dev</a>
        with a deletion request. To help us locate and remove the right data,
        please include:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>the email address or account name you used with GoZeroShot</li>
        <li>which platform(s) you connected (e.g. TikTok, LinkedIn, Meta/Facebook/Instagram)</li>
        <li>the username, Page, Board, or channel name associated with the connection, if known</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Never include passwords, tokens, secrets, cookies, recovery codes, or
        OAuth authorization codes in a deletion request — GoZeroShot will
        never ask for these, and they are not needed to process a deletion.
      </p>

      <h2>Disconnecting at the platform</h2>
      <p>
        You can revoke GoZeroShot's access at the source at any time by going
        to the connected platform's own app/connection settings (for example,
        the platform's "Apps," "Connected Accounts," or "Third-Party Access"
        page) and removing GoZeroShot from the list of authorized apps. This
        stops GoZeroShot from making further API calls on that account
        immediately.
      </p>

      <h2>Stored data vs. published content</h2>
      <p>
        Deleting the integration data GoZeroShot stores (account identifiers,
        authorization scopes, cached drafts, retrieved analytics, and similar
        records) is different from deleting content that has already been
        published to a platform. Removing published posts, pins, videos, or
        ads requires deleting them directly on that platform — GoZeroShot
        deleting its own records does not reach into the platform to remove
        that content.
      </p>

      <h2>Timing</h2>
      <p>
        We process deletion requests as soon as reasonably possible after we
        can verify the request. We do not currently commit to a fixed
        deletion deadline; if you need confirmation once a specific request
        is complete, ask in your email and we will confirm.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Data deletion requests and questions can be sent to
        <a href="mailto:alynch@gozeroshot.dev">alynch@gozeroshot.dev</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    display: block;
  }

  .legal-shell {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
    border-radius: 18px;
    padding: 2rem;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: #4a6f98;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 2.2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  h2 {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }

  p {
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
  }

  ul {
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 0.9rem 1.25rem;
  }

  li {
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .effective-date {
    color: #6b7280;
  }
</style>
